-- title:
--   Stalks over an affine chart: germs of chart functions and constants generate up to units
-- statement:
--   Let $R$, $A$, $O$ be commutative rings in a fixed universe with $A$ and $O$ algebras over $R$, let $X$ be a scheme, $f \colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ a morphism, and $i \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to X$ an open immersion with $i$ followed by $f$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $R \to A$. Form the base change $P = X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} O$ along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R \to O$, and let $x$ be a point of $P$ lying in the preimage under the first projection of the open image $i(\top)$ of $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Then for every germ $s$ in the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{P,x}$ there exist $u, w \in \mathcal{O}_{P,x}$ with $w$ a unit, $s \cdot w = u$, and both $u$ and $w$ lying in the subring of $\mathcal{O}_{P,x}$ generated by the union of two families: the germs at $x$ of the sections over $i(\top)^{-1}$ obtained by pulling back along the first projection the section of $\mathcal{O}_X$ on $i(\top)$ corresponding to $a \in A$ under the global-sections identifications, for $a$ ranging over $A$; and the germs at $x$ of the global sections of $P$ obtained by pulling back along the second projection the element $o \in \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} O, \top)$, for $o$ ranging over $O$.
--
--   This is the elementwise, isomorphism-free expression of the fact that the part of the base change lying over an affine chart $\operatorname{Spec} A \subseteq X$ is $\operatorname{Spec}(A \otimes_R O)$, whose stalk at $x$ is a localisation of $A \otimes_R O$, so that every germ becomes, after multiplication by a unit, a polynomial expression in the germs of chart functions and of constants from $O$. In this form it is used in the construction of Deligne–Rapoport model packages for modular curves, where a ring homomorphism out of such a stalk has to be recognised from its values on chart functions and on constants.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_exists_isUnit_mul_eq_mem_closure_of_stalk_pullback.lean

